WEBVTT

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:08.780
The final Promotion Battle before the start
of the Masters Tournament is nearly upon us.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:11.120
The match-up is between
the following two...

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:12.950
Currently ranked 8th,

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:19.080
the strongest Gym Leader in Galar’s Pokémon League,
and a user of Dragon types: Competitor Kibana.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.460
His opponent
is currently ranked 9th...

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:27.470
...and climbing the ranks with incredible momentum.
The promising new star from Kanto: Competitor Satoshi.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.010
Satoshi’s amazing!
Look at all the attention he’s getting!

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:32.220
‘Course he is!

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.680
The Championships are
a worldwide tournament, after all.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.560
This is really cool.
Imagine if he ends up winning the whole thing.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.480
It wouldn’t exactly be easy.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.900
After all,
he’s facing the Masters Eight.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:49.610
The Champion, Competitor Dande,
had some words to say about their battle.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:52.530
They’re both strong trainers,
with strong Pokémon.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:56.120
I’m sure we’ll get to see a heated battle
far beyond our expectations.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.500
Their battle will be...

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.750
...one we should all make
every effort to enjoy!

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.380
I’m getting really excited!

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:08.300
By the way,
where is Satoshi?

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.970
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.600
Great work, Negigaknight!

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.390
Gänger! Shadow Ball!

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:18.810
Uonoragon, use Jaw Bite!

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.650
Lucario! Shadow Clones!

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:29.820
Kairyu, use Hurricane!

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.950
He’s hard at work!

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:38.290
That’s really intense...

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:39.290
Aura Sphere!

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:48.880
Hey!
We brought you some snacks!

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.260
How about a break?

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.300
Oh, thanks!
Nice timing!

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.970
Let’s have a break, everyone!

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:16.120
Lucario’s really raring to go!

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:17.030
Yeah!

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:20.370
I know exactly what
Lucario’s thinking!

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.460
He still wants to get stronger!

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:25.500
Eevee?!

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.090
What?

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.510
Even Keromatsu
is battling, huh?

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:41.140
It’s evolving!

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:50.230
Gekogashira’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:51.860
All right!

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:52.490
Ooh...

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.370
Lucario!
Let’s go see <i>him!</i>

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.750
Let’s go see Gekkouga!

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.390
Satoshi and Go
decided to visit Gekkouga,

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.440
so that Lucario may yet
improve himself even more.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.980
Their destination:
the Kalos region.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:59.400
Gekkouga! Shinobi Pokémon!
Water/Evil type!

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.280
It creates shuriken
out of compressed water!

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:06.490
When it spins them and throws them at high speed,
they can split metal in two!

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.960
That’s so cool!

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:13.590
So... I get that you traveled
across Kalos with Gekkouga,

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:15.170
but why take Lucario to him?

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:17.090
Back then,
when I got all fired up battling,

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:20.130
it was like I became Gekkouga
and Gekkouga became me!

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:20.630
Huh?

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:26.010
And the way Lucario’s Aura feels
kinda reminds me of that.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.640
So I wanna have them meet up!

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.560
What do you think, Lucario?

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:36.400
Whoa, it’s the real Kibana!

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.900
Ah...!
Thank you so much!

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:43.660
Mr. Kibana!
It’s my dream to be a trainer just like you!

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:44.660
Is it, now?

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:46.410
Keep at it!

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:46.910
I will!

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:52.170
We’ll come and cheer for you
at your next battle!

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.920
Win the match for us, please!

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.300
You think I’d ever lose?

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:09.180
That trainer who wowed Dande...

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:12.940
Never thought
he’d rise up this quickly.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:22.150
“Win the match for us, please!”, huh?

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:28.030
That was a great battle!
Let’s have another one sometime!

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:37.750
What a pathetic face...

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:40.550
How could I let myself...?

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:50.890
I can’t forget that regret.

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:53.480
That’s why I started taking selfies.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.860
I’ll be the one to topple Dande.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:00.480
I’ve come too far
to lose now.

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.690
Let’s go! Duraludon!

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:08.830
So... Where is Gekkouga?

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:10.620
Somewhere in this forest!

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:14.160
H-Hey, hold on!

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:38.150
After all that,
we didn’t find him.

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:40.650
Is Gekkouga really even here?

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:42.280
He is!

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:43.650
I know he is!

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:47.570
Gekkouga and me...

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.660
We’re always connected,
even if we’re apart.

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:54.950
Keromatsu was the first Pokémon
I caught when I arrived in Kalos,

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:58.210
and we got stronger together
as we traveled.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:03.590
At one point we even fought,
‘cause I was too focused on winning a battle...

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:05.630
But we made peace again.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:10.470
After that, we made it all the way
to the Kalos League finals.

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:16.270
Then, Gekkouga stayed here
to protect Kalos.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.650
I bet he’s gotten
a lot stronger since.

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:22.690
I hope we find him soon.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:23.860
Yeah!

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:42.840
It’s Gekkouga!

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:45.880
Lucario, did you feel that, too?

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.130
Huh? What?

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:51.840
Lucario!

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:54.260
Satoshi! Wait for me!

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:49.570
Lucario! Aura Sphere!

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:55.700
Satoshi!

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:59.080
What is all this?!

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:02.460
Go!

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:09.840
Gekkouga!

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:25.810
Let’s go, Gekkouga!

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.190
Shadow Clones!

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:33.150
Whoa...

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:39.620
I can feel it...

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.040
There!

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:49.090
Water Shuriken!

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:04.560
Gekkouga!

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:06.560
How’ve you been?!

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:14.070
Gekkouga...

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:16.610
He really <i>is</i> cool...

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:24.000
Gekkouga...

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:25.750
Have a battle with us!

00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:37.340
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:49.480
We wanna get stronger!

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:53.740
Gekkouga! If we can battle you,
I just know we’ll learn something!

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.460
You’ll do it?

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:10.920
All right! Here we go, Lucario!

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:18.930
How’s this battle going to go?

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:27.100
Lucario! To your right!

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:30.940
Your left!

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:36.990
I didn’t see a thing...

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:41.490
Shadow Clones!

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:46.500
They both used Shadow Clones?!

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:51.500
Lucario!

00:13:04.390 --> 00:13:05.430
Stop, Lucario!

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.580
You want to Mega Evolve?

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:25.660
All right...

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:33.750
Lucario!

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:41.760
Lucario...

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:51.230
Lucario!

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:55.730
Gekkouga...

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:06.490
Satoshi, you’re not going to
chase after Lucario?

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:07.620
Nah!

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:10.040
We can leave this to Gekkouga!

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:08.180
...Lucario and Gekkouga are similar?

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:09.430
Yeah.

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:12.810
They’ve both been all about getting stronger
since I met them.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:15.690
I heard their feelings loud and clear.

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:17.190
Huh...

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:19.020
And not through words...

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:21.940
They rang out loud,
deep in here!

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:29.010
I wonder how far they went...

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:31.300
They’ll come back soon.

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:52.080
There are more?!

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.580
Pikachu! Lightning Speed!

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:58.870
Aceburn, use Pyro Ball!

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:05.130
100,000 Volts!

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:16.350
It’s bigger than the one from before!

00:17:16.350 --> 00:17:17.930
Not good...

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:28.650
Gekkouga! Lucario!

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:31.070
All right! Shadow Clones!

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:33.410
Gekkouga, you use Slicing Draw!

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:38.040
Go!

00:17:44.340 --> 00:17:45.300
I can feel it!

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.380
Lucario’s Aura!

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:50.550
Aura Sphere!

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.140
Not enough!

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:03.650
Let’s go, Lucario!

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:09.150
The bond between us...

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:12.660
Mega Evolve!

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:34.390
Shadow Clones!

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:51.280
Incredible teamwork!

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:55.780
Gekkouga, go for it!

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:00.290
Lucario, we can do this!

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:11.050
Aura Sphere!

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:19.560
That’s it, Lucario!

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:27.060
More... Give it more!

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:56.680
Now!

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:24.950
Wh-Whoa...

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:33.960
You did it!

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:43.810
Wai— Lucario!

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:51.400
Thank you, Gekkouga.

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:53.530
See you again someday.

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:55.440
Take care of yourself till then!

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:11.290
He’s already gone...

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.090
Even if we’re far apart...

00:21:13.090 --> 00:21:15.300
I’m always connected
to Gekkouga.

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:18.630
Same for you, Lucario!

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:25.850
Satoshi has witnessed Lucario
improve himself even more.

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:27.100
And his opponent is...

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:34.570
I’ll be the one to topple Dande
and become Champion!

00:21:37.070 --> 00:21:38.650
Satoshi and Kibana!

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:41.990
They’re about to clash
for a seat in the Masters Eight!

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:09.580
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:11.540 --> 00:23:14.420
The Masters Eight Promotion Match!
It’s here!

00:23:14.420 --> 00:23:16.130
You’re facing Mr. Kibana.

00:23:16.130 --> 00:23:18.040
You <i>do</i> have a plan, right?

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:18.630
Yeah!

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:21.460
I’ll go “Boom!”, and I’ll go “Bash!”,
and “Whoosh-whoosh-whoosh!”...

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:23.130
You’ll need
more than that to beat—

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:26.640
“Bam! Ba-bam! Shiiing!”
...and I’ll win for sure!

00:23:26.640 --> 00:23:28.100
S-Sure...

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:29.680
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:29.680 --> 00:23:33.600
VS Kibana!
The Battle for the Masters Eight!!
